---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Affiliate disclosure | Top Picks"
  description="How Top Picks is funded: affiliate commissions, what that does and does not change, and how to read the ranking with that in mind."
  path="/disclosure"
>
  <main class="wrap prose">
    <div class="kicker">Disclosure</div>
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p>
      Top Picks participates in affiliate programs run by hosting, domain, and
      email marketing companies.
      That means some links on this site — especially “Visit” and “Go to” buttons — are
      tracking links. If you click one and later buy a plan, the company may pay us a
      commission.
    </p>
    <p>
      You should not pay a higher price because you came through this site. The commission
      comes from the provider, not from an extra line on your bill. Free trials, coupons,
      and renewal rates are still the provider’s terms.
    </p>
    <h2>What this does not mean</h2>
    <p>
      It does not mean a host can buy a #1 badge. Rank order is an editorial call based
      on the <a href="/methodology">method</a>: who the product is for, how hard it is
      to start, and how honest the pricing is after the intro period.
    </p>
    <p>
      It also does not mean every outbound link is affiliate. Where a program is missing
      or a page is not a product we recommend for a purchase, we link to the public site
      without tracking.
    </p>
    <h2>How to read the ranking anyway</h2>
    <p>
      Assume we benefit if you click. Then ask whether the write-up still holds: does
      the host match the badge, and did we flag the renewal. If the answer is no, ignore
      the button. The reviews are meant to be usable even if you type the brand into
      a search bar yourself.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is an opinionated consumer guide, not financial, legal, or uptime advice,
      and not a guarantee that any provider will stay online or keep its current pricing.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
